course: dictionary
lesson: 15168
title: Scraps: bits left over
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer wants. The word scraps can mean small pieces, bits of food, or a small fight. Look at the clues around it.
explain: «The hens ate the food scraps from our dinner.» The word food is the clue, so scraps means bits of food left after a meal. «Mum swept up the scraps of paper.» Paper is the clue, so scraps means small pieces of paper.
explain: Scraps can also be a doing word. «The team scraps the plan and tries a new one.» Here scraps means throws away. Check by swapping in throws away: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Scraps are small pieces of something, often left over.
fact: «Food scraps» are bits of food left after a meal.
fact: «Scrap metal» is old metal collected so it can be used again.
fact: A «scrap» can also be a small fight, as in «two boys got into a scrap».
fact: As a verb, «scraps» means throws away, as in «she scraps the idea».
exercise: «The hens gobbled up the food scraps.» What are scraps here? | *Bits of food left after a meal | A quiet, gentle breeze | A tall building | Long, thin pieces of wood
exercise: «The old fridge was taken away as scrap metal.» What is scrap metal? | *Old metal collected so it can be used again | Metal that is brand new from the shop | Shiny metal used only for jewellery
exercise: «Two boys got into a scrap in the playground.» What is a scrap here? | A quiet talk | A small meal | *A small fight | A long walk
test: «Mum cut the scraps of cloth for our class collage.» What are the scraps? | Large rolls of cloth | Clean socks | Wet paint | *Small pieces of cloth
test: «He scraps the plan and starts again.» What does scraps mean here? | Makes bigger | Reads aloud | Copies carefully | *Throws away
exam: In «The cat was hungry and lived on table scraps», what does scraps mean? | *Bits of food left after a meal | Old metal collected to be used again | Throws away | Small fights
